    "multilingualFamilyContext": "Many households in Nashville navigate multilingual environments (including English and English). Research confirms that multilingualism does not cause speech delay, autism, or ADHD. Our guidance helps parents foster rich, communicative home environments that honour and nurture all the languages spoken in the family.",
    "schoolSystemOverview": "In Nashville and across the United States, school support for neurodivergent learners is primarily structured under federal frameworks: Individualized Education Programs (IEPs) under IDEA and Section 504 Accommodation Plans. Parents frequently navigate Student Study Team (SST) meetings, comprehensive psychoeducational evaluations, and specialized classroom placements. Online parent consultation helps you understand clinical testing metrics, prioritize requested accommodations, and maintain collaborative dialogue with teachers and school psychologists.",
    "healthcareNavigationOverview": "Families in Nashville seeking formal diagnostic evaluations for ADHD, autism, or related developmental profiles typically consult local developmental paediatricians, child psychiatrists, or registered clinical psychologists. Because regional public and private diagnostic waitlists can extend from several months to over a year, online parent guidance provides vital interim support—delivering evidence-based behavioral strategies, emotional regulation tools, and structured routines from home while awaiting local clinical evaluations.",
    "assessmentWaitingSupport": "While on waiting lists for developmental assessments in Nashville, families can make significant progress at home. You can document specific behavioral triggers across different settings, maintain consistent daily sleep and nutrition routines, request objective observations from classroom teachers, and implement positive, proactive co-regulation strategies to support emotional well-being.",
