    "culturalContext": "Families in Southampton balance demanding work schedules with high academic and extracurricular commitments. In multicultural urban communities, parents often navigate diverse cultural expectations alongside Western educational systems. Our parent guidance sessions respect your family's distinct values while applying globally recognized, evidence-based developmental strategies.",
    "multilingualFamilyContext": "Many households in Southampton navigate multilingual environments (including English and English). Research confirms that multilingualism does not cause speech delay, autism, or ADHD. Our guidance helps parents foster rich, communicative home environments that honour and nurture all the languages spoken in the family.",
    "schoolSystemOverview": "In Southampton and throughout the UK, educational support is guided by the Special Educational Needs and Disability (SEND) Code of Practice. Schools implement graduated support via SEN Support plans and Education, Health and Care Plans (EHCPs), coordinated by the school Special Educational Needs Coordinator (SENCO). With lengthy local authority assessment waiting times, parent consultation equips you to prepare clear documentary evidence, formulate targeted classroom adaptations, and navigate annual reviews effectively.",
    "healthcareNavigationOverview": "Families in Southampton seeking formal diagnostic evaluations for ADHD, autism, or related developmental profiles typically consult local developmental paediatricians, child psychiatrists, or registered clinical psychologists. Because regional public and private diagnostic waitlists can extend from several months to over a year, online parent guidance provides vital interim support—delivering evidence-based behavioral strategies, emotional regulation tools, and structured routines from home while awaiting local clinical evaluations.",
    "assessmentWaitingSupport": "While on waiting lists for developmental assessments in Southampton, families can make significant progress at home. You can document specific behavioral triggers across different settings, maintain consistent daily sleep and nutrition routines, request objective observations from classroom teachers, and implement positive, proactive co-regulation strategies to support emotional well-being.",
    "practicalParentGuidance": [
      "Break multi-step verbal instructions into single, sequential visual or auditory cues.",
      "Implement predictable visual schedules for morning routines and homework transitions.",
      "Prioritize emotional co-regulation during intense moments before attempting problem-solving.",
      "Create a low-distraction, sensory-friendly homework and decompression area at home.",
      "Maintain an objective home-school communication log to track patterns over time."
    ],
