    "culturalContext": "Families in Hamilton balance demanding work schedules with high academic and extracurricular commitments. In multicultural urban communities, parents often navigate diverse cultural expectations alongside Western educational systems. Our parent guidance sessions respect your family's distinct values while applying globally recognized, evidence-based developmental strategies.",
    "multilingualFamilyContext": "Many households in Hamilton navigate multilingual environments (including English and English). Research confirms that multilingualism does not cause speech delay, autism, or ADHD. Our guidance helps parents foster rich, communicative home environments that honour and nurture all the languages spoken in the family.",
    "schoolSystemOverview": "In Hamilton and across Canada, provincial ministries of education provide Individual Education Plans (IEPs) and Identification, Placement, and Review Committee (IPRC) frameworks. Schools collaborate with multidisciplinary resource teachers to implement classroom accommodations and modified curriculums. Parent consultation assists families in interpreting school psychoeducational evaluations and establishing cohesive home-school routines.",
    "healthcareNavigationOverview": "Families in Hamilton seeking formal diagnostic evaluations for ADHD, autism, or related developmental profiles typically consult local developmental paediatricians, child psychiatrists, or registered clinical psychologists. Because regional public and private diagnostic waitlists can extend from several months to over a year, online parent guidance provides vital interim support—delivering evidence-based behavioral strategies, emotional regulation tools, and structured routines from home while awaiting local clinical evaluations.",
    "assessmentWaitingSupport": "While on waiting lists for developmental assessments in Hamilton, families can make significant progress at home. You can document specific behavioral triggers across different settings, maintain consistent daily sleep and nutrition routines, request objective observations from classroom teachers, and implement positive, proactive co-regulation strategies to support emotional well-being.",
    "practicalParentGuidance": [
      "Break multi-step verbal instructions into single, sequential visual or auditory cues.",
      "Implement predictable visual schedules for morning routines and homework transitions.",
      "Prioritize emotional co-regulation during intense moments before attempting problem-solving.",
      "Create a low-distraction, sensory-friendly homework and decompression area at home.",
      "Maintain an objective home-school communication log to track patterns over time."
    ],
