    "culturalContext": "In Mingora, family life often centres around close-knit, multigenerational households. While extended family involvement provides immense warmth and daily support, differing generational views on developmental milestones, attention, and discipline can sometimes create parental stress. Our consultations provide a compassionate, culturally respectful space in English or Urdu to build unified home strategies.",
    "multilingualFamilyContext": "Many households in Mingora navigate multilingual environments (including Urdu and English). Research confirms that multilingualism does not cause speech delay, autism, or ADHD. Our guidance helps parents foster rich, communicative home environments that honour and nurture all the languages spoken in the family.",
    "schoolSystemOverview": "In Mingora and throughout Pakistan, education spans provincial public institutions, semi-private networks, and private Cambridge/international schools. While formal special education legislation is evolving, many schools offer specialized learning-support coordinators and individualized accommodations. Online parent guidance helps parents communicate constructively with educators, structure homework expectations, and create clear collaborative plans.",
    "healthcareNavigationOverview": "Families in Mingora seeking formal diagnostic evaluations for ADHD, autism, or related developmental profiles typically consult local developmental paediatricians, child psychiatrists, or registered clinical psychologists. Because regional public and private diagnostic waitlists can extend from several months to over a year, online parent guidance provides vital interim support—delivering evidence-based behavioral strategies, emotional regulation tools, and structured routines from home while awaiting local clinical evaluations.",
    "assessmentWaitingSupport": "While on waiting lists for developmental assessments in Mingora, families can make significant progress at home. You can document specific behavioral triggers across different settings, maintain consistent daily sleep and nutrition routines, request objective observations from classroom teachers, and implement positive, proactive co-regulation strategies to support emotional well-being.",
    "practicalParentGuidance": [
      "Break multi-step verbal instructions into single, sequential visual or auditory cues.",
      "Implement predictable visual schedules for morning routines and homework transitions.",
      "Prioritize emotional co-regulation during intense moments before attempting problem-solving.",
      "Create a low-distraction, sensory-friendly homework and decompression area at home.",
      "Maintain an objective home-school communication log to track patterns over time."
    ],
