    "culturalContext": "In Brussels, families benefit from supportive community structures while navigating distinct cultural and educational expectations. Our parent guidance sessions respect your unique family dynamic and heritage, delivering evidence-based developmental strategies that align with your daily life in Belgium.",
    "multilingualFamilyContext": "Many households in Brussels navigate multilingual environments (including Dutch and English). Research confirms that multilingualism does not cause speech delay, autism, or ADHD. Our guidance helps parents foster rich, communicative home environments that honour and nurture all the languages spoken in the family.",
    "schoolSystemOverview": "In Brussels and across Belgium, education systems provide inclusive learning support and specialized pedagogical accommodations for children with learning differences and attention needs. Whether attending international baccalaureate (IB), national bilingual, or local community schools, our consultations help parents understand school reports and collaborate productively with learning-support teams.",
    "healthcareNavigationOverview": "Families in Brussels seeking formal diagnostic evaluations for ADHD, autism, or related developmental profiles typically consult local developmental paediatricians, child psychiatrists, or registered clinical psychologists. Because regional public and private diagnostic waitlists can extend from several months to over a year, online parent guidance provides vital interim support—delivering evidence-based behavioral strategies, emotional regulation tools, and structured routines from home while awaiting local clinical evaluations.",
    "assessmentWaitingSupport": "While on waiting lists for developmental assessments in Brussels, families can make significant progress at home. You can document specific behavioral triggers across different settings, maintain consistent daily sleep and nutrition routines, request objective observations from classroom teachers, and implement positive, proactive co-regulation strategies to support emotional well-being.",
    "practicalParentGuidance": [
      "Break multi-step verbal instructions into single, sequential visual or auditory cues.",
      "Implement predictable visual schedules for morning routines and homework transitions.",
      "Prioritize emotional co-regulation during intense moments before attempting problem-solving.",
      "Create a low-distraction, sensory-friendly homework and decompression area at home.",
      "Maintain an objective home-school communication log to track patterns over time."
    ],
