    "schoolSystemOverview": "In Zurich and across Switzerland, education systems provide inclusive learning support and specialized pedagogical accommodations for children with learning differences and attention needs. Whether attending international baccalaureate (IB), national bilingual, or local community schools, our consultations help parents understand school reports and collaborate productively with learning-support teams.",
    "healthcareNavigationOverview": "Families in Zurich seeking formal diagnostic evaluations for ADHD, autism, or related developmental profiles typically consult local developmental paediatricians, child psychiatrists, or registered clinical psychologists. Because regional public and private diagnostic waitlists can extend from several months to over a year, online parent guidance provides vital interim support—delivering evidence-based behavioral strategies, emotional regulation tools, and structured routines from home while awaiting local clinical evaluations.",
    "assessmentWaitingSupport": "While on waiting lists for developmental assessments in Zurich, families can make significant progress at home. You can document specific behavioral triggers across different settings, maintain consistent daily sleep and nutrition routines, request objective observations from classroom teachers, and implement positive, proactive co-regulation strategies to support emotional well-being.",
